##DESCRIPTION
## SHM calculations
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Mechanics)
## DBchapter(Oscillations)
## DBsection(Simple Harmonic Motion)
## Date(29 December 2017)
## Institution(Brock University)
## Author(Santo D'Agostino)
## TitleText('')
## AuthorText('')
## EditionText('2018')
## Section('16.3')
## Problem('14')
## KEYWORDS(frequency, period, kinematics, simple harmonic motion)

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric')->variables->are(t => 'Real');

$X     = random(5,   20);
$f     = random(0.5, 0.95, 0.05);
$T     = 1 / $f;
$pos   = Compute("$X cos(2 pi $f t)");
$vel   = $pos->D('t');
$accel = $vel->D('t');

@t  = (1 .. 4);
@x  = map { $pos->eval(t => $_) } @t;
@v  = map { $vel->eval(t => $_) } @t;
@a  = map { $accel->eval(t => $_) } @t;
$x5 = random(-$X, $X, 0.1);
do { $v6 = random(-20, 20, 0.1) } until (abs($v6) < 2 * pi * $f * $X);
do { $a7 = random(-30, 30, 0.1) } until (abs($a7) < 4 * (pi**2) * ($f**2) * $X);
$t5 = (1 / (2 * pi * $f)) * arccos($x5 / $X);
$t6 = (1 / (2 * pi * $f)) * arcsin($v6 / (-2 * pi * $f * $X));
$t7 = (1 / (2 * pi * $f)) * arccos($a7 / (-4 * (pi**2) * ($f**2) * $X));
$v8 = 2 * pi * $f * $X;
$a9 = 4 * (pi**2) * ($f**2) * $X;
$k  = random(25, 50, 0.5);
$m  = $k / ((2 * pi * $f)**2);

BEGIN_PGML
A block attached to the end of a spring moves in simple harmonic motion according to the position function
[```
x(t) = X \cos \left ( 2\pi f \cdot t\right )
```]
where the frequency of the motion is [`[$f]`] Hz and the amplitude of the motion is [`[$X]`] cm.

a) State the value of [`X`]. [_]{$X} [`\textrm{cm}`]

b) State the value of [`f`]. [_]{$f} [`\textrm{Hz}`]

c) Determine the period of the motion. [_]{$T} [`\textrm{s}`]

d) Fill in the table with the position of the block at the given value of [`t`]:

    [# [. [`t`] .][. [`x(t)`] .]*{headerrow => 1}
    [. [` 1\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$x[0]} .]*
    [. [` 2\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$x[1]} .]*
    [. [` 3\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$x[2]} .]*
    [. [` 4\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$x[3]} .]* #]{align=>'|c|c|',
        horizontalrules => 1, padding => 0.25}

e) Fill in the table with the velocity of the block at the given value of [`t`]:

    [# [. [`t`] .][. [`v(t)`] .]*{headerrow => 1}
    [. [` 1\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$v[0]} .]*
    [. [` 2\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$v[1]} .]*
    [. [` 3\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$v[2]} .]*
    [. [` 4\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$v[3]} .]* #]{align=>'|c|c|', 
        horizontalrules => 1, padding => 0.25}

f) Fill in the table with the acceleration of the block at the given value of [`t`]:

    [# [. [`t`] .][. [`a(t)`] .]*{headerrow => 1}
    [. [` 1\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$a[0]} .]*
    [. [` 2\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$a[1]} .]*
    [. [` 3\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$a[2]} .]*
    [. [` 4\textrm{s}`].] [. [_]{$a[3]} .]* #]{align=>'|c|c|', 
        horizontalrules => 1, padding => 0.25}

g) Determine the first time at which the position of the block is [`[$x5]`] cm.

    [_]{$t5} [`\textrm{s}`]

h) Determine the first time at which the velocity of the block is [`[$v6]`] cm/s.

    [_]{$t6} [`\textrm{s}`]

i) Determine the first time at which the acceleration of the block is [`[$a7]`] cm/s<sup>2</sup>.

    [_]{$t7} [`\textrm{s}`]

j) Determine the maximum speed of the block. [_]{$v8} [`\textrm{cm}/\textrm{s}`]

k) Determine the magnitude of the maximum acceleration of the block.

    [_]{$a9} [`\textrm{cm}/\textrm{s}^2`]

l) Suppose that the stiffness constant of the spring is [`[$k]`] N/m. Determine the mass of the block.

    [_]{$m} [`\textrm{kg}`]
END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();
